  "term": "MLE",
  "definition": "MLE stands for maximum likelihood estimation, a statistical approach used here to build a model that estimates perceptual differences from sorting-task responses. In this context, it is presented as a way to balance efficiency and accuracy when measuring perceptual discrimination.",
